0000:                   ********************************************************************
0000:                   * RBF - Random Block File Manager
0000:                   *
0000:                   * $Id$
0000:                   *
0000:                   * Modified for 6309 Native mode by Bill Nobel, L. Curtis Boyle & Wes Gale
0000:                   *
0000:                   * This also contains the patch for un-deleting files
0000:                   *
0000:                   * Undocumented SetStt/GetStt calls:
0000:                   *
0000:                   *     GetStt:
0000:                   *         SS.FD ($0F) - Returns a file descriptor
0000:                   *                          Entry: R$A=Path #
0000:                   *                                 R$B=SS.FD ($0F)
0000:                   *                                 R$X=Pointer to a 256 byte buffer
0000:                   *                                 R$Y=# bytes of FD required
0000:                   *         SS.FDInf ($20) - Directly reads a file descriptor from anywhere
0000:                   *                          on drive.
0000:                   *                          Entry: R$A=Path #
0000:                   *                                 R$B=SS.FDInf ($20)
0000:                   *                                 R$X=Pointer to a 256 byte buffer
0000:                   *                                 R$Y= MSB - Length of read
0000:                   *                                      LSB - MSB of logical sector #
0000:                   *                                 R$U= LSW of logical sector #
0000:                   *     SetStt:
0000:                   *         SS.FD ($0F) - Writes a file descriptor
0000:                   *                          Entry: R$A=Path #
0000:                   *                                 R$B=SS.FD ($0F)
0000:                   *                                 R$X=Pointer to a maximum 256 byte buffer
0000:                   *                                 R$Y=# bytes of FD to write
0000:                   *         SS.Ticks ($10) - Set # ticks to wait for record lock release
0000:                   *                          Entry: R$A=Path #
0000:                   *                                 R$B=SS.Ticks ($10)
0000:                   *                                 R$X=# Ticks to wait
0000:                   *         SS.Lock ($11) - Force Lock/Release of a file.
0000:                   *                         Locks from current position to a specified size
0000:                   *                          Entry: R$A=Path #
0000:                   *                                 R$B=SS.Lock ($11)
0000:                   *                                 R$X=LSW of end byte position
0000:                   *                                 R$U=MSW of end byte position
0000:                   *         SS.Attr ($1C) - Allows changing of file/directory attributes
0000:                   *                         If changing directory attribute it scans to
0000:                   *                         see if directory is empty.
0000:                   *                          Entry: R$A=Path #
0000:                   *                                 R$B=SS.Attr ($1C)
0000:                   *                                 R$X= LSB - File attributes
0000:                   *         SS.RsBit ($1E) - Reserve bitmap sector (doesn't allocate)
0000:                   *                          Locks the bitmap sector from other programs
0000:                   *                          so they cannot allocate in it.
0000:                   *                          Useful when working in allocation map.
0000:                   *                          Entry: R$A=Path #
0000:                   *                                 R$B=SS.RsBit ($1E)
0000:                   *                                 R$X= LSB - Sector # of bitmap
0000:                   *
0000:                   * Edt/Rev  YYYY/MM/DD  Modified by
0000:                   * Comment
0000:                   * ------------------------------------------------------------------
0000:                   *          1993/09/19  ???
0000:                   * Started putting in comments from buggy 1.09 code, fixed WP error
0000:                   * bug on file delete, fixed FD read error bug in delete.
0000:                   *
0000:                   *          1994/07/15  ???
0000:                   * Fixed long overdue LHA bug; modified M$Exec driver calls @ L11EB
0000:                   * to use V$DRIVEX.
0000:                   *
0000:                   *          1994/07/27  ???
0000:                   * Changed L11EB to just PSHS/PULS A,X,PC instead of D,X,PC (saves
0000:                   * 2 cycles per driver call); changed BRA L12C6 @ L128E to PULS PC,U,X
0000:                   *
0000:                   *          ????/??/??  ???
0000:                   * NitrOS-9 2.00 distribution.
0000:                   *
0000:                   *  35      ????/??/??  Gene Heskett
0000:                   * Fixed FD.SEG bug.
0000:                   *
0000:                   *          2003/04/21  Boisy G. Pitre
0000:                   * Folded RBF 30 comments into this version.
0000:                   *
0000:                   *  36      2003/05/01  Rodney V. Hamilton
0000:                   * Fix for LSN0 DD.TOT=0 lockout problem
0000:                   *
0000:                   *  37      2004/06/18  Boisy G. Pitre
0000:                   * Added call to driver's SS.VarSect GetStat in order to obtain the
0000:                   * sector size of the media.
0000:                   *
0000:                   *  37r2    2004/07/18  Boisy G. Pitre
0000:                   * RBF checks error code on return from SS.VarSect and only returns
0000:                   * error if error code is != E$UnkSvc (fixes problems with drivers
0000:                   * which do not support SS.VarSect and return E$UnkSvc in their GetStat
0000:                   * routines after evaluating an unknown service code.)
0000:                   *
0000:                   *  37r3    2009/12/26  Boisy G. Pitre
0000:                   * Moved SS.VarSect code down to fix a problem where code to call driver
0000:                   * expected PD.Exten to be allocated when it wasn't, and that caused
0000:                   * a write to PE.Prior to go into the system globals area (address $0016).
0000:                   
0000:                            nam   RBF
0000:                            ttl   Random Block File Manager
0000:                   
0000:                            ifp1  
0000:                            use   defsfile
0000:                            endc  
0000:                   
0003:                   rev      set   $03
00D0:                   ty       set   FlMgr
0000:                            IFNE  H6309
0001:                   lg       set   Obj6309
0000:                            ELSE
0001:                   lg       set   Objct
0000:                            ENDC
00D1:                   tylg     set   ty+lg
0083:                   atrv     set   ReEnt+rev
0025:                   edition  set   37
0000:                   
0000:                            org   $00
0000:                   size     equ   .
0000:                   
